  "journalText": "The fire returns with a detail the larger account neglected: a cup with a broken handle. The warrior had set it aside. The fourth companion sat beside him and repaired it with a short length of wire, working while the others discussed the road below the kingdom.\n\nThe warrior's loyalty began as a debt he owed the fourth companion.\n\nTheir loyalty grew from small acts freely given, before either man had anything to repay.\n\nThere was no rescue to reward that evening, no oath demanded in exchange. The repaired cup passed between them without ceremony. Later, when the fourth spoke too confidently, the warrior answered him without fear that disagreement would end their place beside the same fire.\n\nThat ordinary freedom matters. A follower might have mistaken certainty for strength. Someone who had shared cold meals and foolish plans could recognize the person beneath it. The warrior would challenge him precisely because the friendship allowed more than obedience. The wire was crooked. The cup held.\n\nBefore he tried to protect his friend from a terrible choice, he had learned that he could tell him no.",
  "wordCount": 185,
  "newlyRecoveredInformation": "Their bond developed through unpriced everyday care, and permitted disagreement before the sanctuary crisis. Loyalty was not repayment for a rescue or allegiance to a leader.",
  "newlyAuthoredDetails": [
    "The fourth companion repairs the warrior's cup beside the campfire.",
    "The cup's crooked wire becomes a mundane memory motif, never a magical artifact."
  ],
